      "writtenOn": "2024-02-09T18:36:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Good question. I\u0027m afraid I don\u0027t have a good answer.\n\nThese environment variables are specific to each workstation. For example, when I SSH into my gLinux workstation, `XDG_RUNTIME_DIR` is set, but `DISPLAY` is not set, even though there is a graphical session running in the background. This means that for my particular setup:\n\n- I can just pipe through `XDG_RUNTIME_DIR` with `--test_env\u003dXDG_RUNTIME_DIR` (note that this is `--test_env\u003dVAR` rather than `--test_env\u003dVAR\u003dVAL`).\n- I need to define the right value for `DISPLAY`, which in my case is `:20`, so I use `--test_env\u003dDISPLAY\u003d:20`.\n\nThere is no guarantee that the right value for `DISPLAY` is going to be `:20` for other folks.\n\nFurthermore, if I open a terminal emulator from within a graphical session, `DISPLAY` will already be set, so I would invoke Bazel with `--test_env\u003dDISPLAY` rather than `--test_env\u003dDISPLAY\u003d:20`.",
      "parentUuid": "d8c2869b_b04de042",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 22,
        "startChar": 10,
        "endLine": 22,
        "endChar": 32
      },
