      "writtenOn": "2024-02-09T18:36:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is just a list comprehension that yields exactly one `cc_test_with_flags` target (i.e. one test binary) per `[name, surfaceConfig]` pair. It is equivalent to writing the following targets explicitly:\n\n```\ncc_test_with_flags(\n    name \u003d \"gpu_vk_test\",\n    srcs \u003d ...,\n    args \u003d [\"--surfaceConfig\", \"vk\", \"--autoTuneLoops\"],\n    ...\n)\n\ncc_test_with_flags(\n    name \u003d \"gpu_vk_1010102_test\",\n    srcs \u003d ...,\n    args \u003d [\"--surfaceConfig\", \"vk_1010102\", \"--autoTuneLoops\"],\n    ...\n)\n\ncc_test_with_flags(\n    name \u003d \"gpu_vk_msaa4_test\",\n    srcs \u003d ...,\n    args \u003d [\"--surfaceConfig\", \"vk_msaa4\", \"--autoTuneLoops\"],\n    ...\n)\n\n...\n```",
